## The other two files

**`Plans-backlog.md`** — unscheduled capture. Plain bullets with a capture date, and
**no `cc:` markers at all**. No counter reads it, and the absence of markers means
there is nothing to find even if one is pointed at it by mistake. Do not add a
`cc:backlog` state: it would put the backlog back into the progress numbers and undo
the reason the file is separate. Promotion into `Plans.md` is a manual rewrite as a
full table row — the friction is deliberate.

**`.claude/memory/archive/Plans-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`** — where terminal rows land. Never
scanned by any counter. Physical separation is far cheaper to enforce than teaching
four separate counters to skip a section, and a single archive *sentence* once inflated
the done count by one.

Archiving is the job of the sweep (`scripts/plans-sweep.sh`), which **proposes and never
writes**. Do not hand-move rows out to make the file look tidy: an archive that doubles
as a hiding place for uncomfortable work stops being a record.

